\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By Associated Press and Reuters \par \uc2 477 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 January 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 AVIATION\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  Took $3 Billion Hit After Strike and Job Cuts\par \par \uc2 Boeing Co.\uc2  said it incurred nearly $3 billion worth of charges in the fourth quarter of 2024 due to a lengthy labor stoppage, job cuts and problems with a number of government programs.\par \par \uc2 As a result, the Chicago-based aerospace giant said Thursday that it will report a loss of $5.46 per share next week when it issues its full financial results. Wall Street had been expecting a fourth-quarter loss of $1.80 per share.\par \par \uc2 The sizable loss caps a rough year for \uc2 Boeing\uc2 . A strike by the machinists who assemble the 737 Max, along with the 777 jet and the 767 cargo plane at factories in Washington halted production at those sites and hampered \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's delivery capability.\par \par \uc2 The walkout ended after more than seven weeks when the company agreed to pay raises and improved benefits.\par \par \uc2 The aerospace giant also announced previously it would reduce its work force by 10 percent. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 Consumer Sentiment Dips Amid Higher Price Fears\par \par \uc2 U.S. consumer sentiment weakened in January for the first time in six months amid worries about the labor market and potential higher prices for goods if President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's new administration presses ahead with planned tariffs on imports.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 University of Michigan\uc2  said on Friday that its Consumer Sentiment Index fell to 71.1 this month from a preliminary reading of 73.2 and 74.0 in December. Economists polled by Reuters had expected an unchanged reading. The final survey was closed on Monday, the day when Trump was inaugurated.\par \par \uc2 The decline in sentiment was broad-based and seen across income, wealth and age groups.\par \par \uc2 Consumers' one-year inflation expectations were at 3.3 percent, up from 2.8 percent in December. The 12-month inflation expectations are now above the 2.3 percent to 3.0 percent range. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 INTERNATIONAL\par \par \uc2 Italian Bank Launches Bid To Take Over Larger Peer\par \par \uc2 Italian bank Monte dei Paschi di Siena announced Friday it was launching a 13.3 billion euro ($13.9 billion) takeover bid for larger peer \uc2 Mediobanca\uc2  in a surprise move that could reshape the country's banking sector.\par \par \uc2 The offer values shares in investment bank \uc2 Mediobanca\uc2  at 15.99 euros each, a 5 percent premium on their closing price Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Monte Paschi, Italy's oldest bank, has a market capitalization of about 9 billion euros, while \uc2 Mediobanca\uc2 's market value is about 12.7 billion euros.\par \par \uc2 Under the terms of the offer, \uc2 Mediobanca\uc2  investors would receive 23 shares in Monte Paschi for every 10 \uc2 Mediobanca\uc2  shares they hold.\par \par \uc2 The buyout offer comes after the Italian government moved to re-privatize the once-troubled bank whose largest shareholder has been the Treasury since an expensive bailout in 2017. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250125el1p0004l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
