\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Associated Press and Reuters \par \uc2 453 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 January 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 JOBS\par \par \uc2 More Americans File Unemployment Claims\par \par \uc2 Jobless claims applications ticked up modestly last week, but the total number of Americans collecting unemployment benefits rose to the highest level in more than three years.\par \par \uc2 Applications for jobless benefits rose by 6,000 to 223,000 for the week ending Jan. 18, the Labor Department said Thursday. Analysts were expecting 219,000 new applications.\par \par \uc2 Weekly applications for jobless benefits are considered a proxy for layoffs.\par \par \uc2 The total number of Americans receiving unemployment benefits for the week of Jan. 11 climbed by 46,000 to 1.9 million, the most since November of 2021.\par \par \uc2 The rising level of continuing claims, the total number of Americans collecting jobless benefits, suggests some who are receiving benefits are finding it harder to land new jobs. That could mean demand for workers is waning, even as the economy remains strong. ASSOCIATED PRESS\par \par \uc2 AVIATION\par \par \uc2 GE Aerospace\uc2  Predicts Stronger Profit in 2025\par \par \uc2 GE Aerospace\uc2  on Thursday forecast stronger profit in 2025, saying it is better prepared to meet jet engine demand with progress in resolving supply chain issues that had hobbled production. Fourth-quarter earnings topped Wall Street estimates, boosting the company's shares by 7 percent.\par \par \uc2 Production of LEAP engines, which power \uc2 Airbus\uc2  and \uc2 Boeing\uc2  aircraft, is expected to increase 15 to 20 percent this year after a 10-percent year-on-year decline in 2024. Primary suppliers are now shipping over 90 percent of the committed volume, compared with about 50 percent a year ago, chief executive \uc2 Larry Culp\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 More than 70 percent of \uc2 GE Aerospace\uc2 's commercial engine revenue comes from parts and services. Limited engine supplies have delayed production of newer planes, forcing airlines to keep flying older, less fuel-efficient jets and spend billions on aircraft maintenance. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 Air Products\uc2  Shareholders Unseat Chief Executive\par \par \uc2 Air Products and Chemicals\uc2  shareholders on Thursday handed victory to an activist investor, who had pushed the industrial gases company to replace its 80-year-old chief, by electing three new directors and unseating the chief executive, Seiffolah Ghasemi, from the board.\par \par \uc2 The company said preliminary tallies showed investors elected three of Mantle Ridge Capital Management's four director candidates to the company's nine-member board.\par \par \uc2 Investors reacted positively to the news by pushing up the stock price 1.6 percent, trading at $321.94.\par \par \uc2 The outcome, which bankers and lawyers called a resounding win for Mantle Ridge, ends one of the most fiercely contested board battles in recent memory and raises questions about Mr. Ghasemi's future at \uc2 Air Products\uc2 , as it is highly unusual for a chief executive to be voted off his own board. REUTERS\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250124el1o00050\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
