\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 The Digest\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Associated Press and Reuters \par \uc2 476 \uc2 words\par \uc2 8 January 2025\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2025 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 November Saw Increase\par \par \uc2 In U.S. Job Openings\par \par \uc2 U.S. job openings rose unexpectedly in November, showing companies are still looking for workers even as the labor market has cooled overall.\par \par \uc2 Openings rose to 8.1 million in November, the most since February and up from 7.8 million in October, the Labor Department reported Tuesday. They were down from 8.9 million a year earlier and a peak of 12.2 million in March 2022 as the economy was roaring back from Covid lockdowns. Economists had expected job openings to fall slightly in November.\par \par \uc2 Layoffs rose slightly in November, and the number of people quitting their jobs fell, suggesting that Americans are less confident in their ability to find better jobs.\par \par \uc2 Openings were up in professional and business services and in finance and insurance. They fell in the information industry, which includes publishers and telecommunications. Associated Press\par \par \uc2 M. & A.\par \par \uc2 Getty Images\uc2  to Merge\par \par \uc2 With \uc2 Shutterstock\par \par \uc2 Getty Images\uc2  is buying \uc2 Shutterstock\uc2  to create a $3.7 billion visual content company.\par \par \uc2 The merger comes at a time when companies that use still images are facing increased competition from images generated by artificial intelligence.\par \par \uc2 The companies said on Tuesday that they have complementary portfolios and that a merger will provide customers with a broader array still imagery, video, music, 3-D and other media.\par \par \uc2 ''With the rapid rise in demand for compelling visual content across industries, there has never been a better time for our two businesses to come together,'' the \uc2 Getty Images\uc2  chief executive \uc2 Craig Peters\uc2  said. He will be the C.E.O. of the combined business.\par \par \uc2 ''We are excited by the opportunities we see to expand our creative content library and enhance our product offering to meet diverse customer needs,'' \uc2 Shutterstock\uc2 's chief executive \uc2 Paul Hennessy\uc2  said. Associated Press\par \par \uc2 REGULATIONS\par \par \uc2 C.F.T.C. Chair to Leave When Trump Takes Office\par \par \uc2 The chair of the \uc2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Rostin Behnam\uc2 , right, will step down when President-elect \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  takes office on Jan. 20, the agency said on Tuesday, paving the way for Mr. Trump to appoint his own chief and kick-start a crypto policy overhaul.\par \par \uc2 While the C.F.T.C., which oversees commodity derivatives markets, has traditionally been a junior player in financial policy, it is expected to play a much more prominent role as Trump's administration pushes for more crypto-friendly rules.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump is expected to initially succeed Mr. Behnam with one of the agency's Republican commissioners -- Summer Mersinger or Caroline Pham -- as acting chair.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump's transition team has also been considering external candidates, including former Republican C.F.T.C. Commissioner \uc2 Brian Quintenz\uc2 , according to two people with knowledge of the matter. A permanent chair would need Senate confirmation. Reuters\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020250108el180004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
