\par\par \uc2 Business/Financial Desk; SECTB\par \b \uc2 Thousands Who Deliver For \uc2 Amazon\uc2  Go on Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Noam Scheiber and Santul Nerkar \par \uc2 1,192 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 December 2024\par \uc2 The New York Times\par \uc2 NYTF\par \uc2 Late Edition - Final\par 1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 The New York Times Company.  All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The retail giant said it expected its operations to be largely unaffected by the strike of some drivers at contracting firms \uc2 Amazon\uc2  uses to deliver packages.\par \par \uc2 Workers who deliver packages from seven \uc2 Amazon\uc2  facilities across the country went on strike Thursday morning, according to the \uc2 International Brotherhood of Teamsters\uc2 , the union that represents them.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said thousands of workers had struck, but it was unclear how many people were participating in the action. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said it expected the seven delivery hubs to operate normally.\par \par \uc2 The drivers are employees of companies that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  uses to deliver packages to customers. \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has said it has no obligation to bargain with the drivers because they are not its employees. But the union and the workers said \uc2 Amazon\uc2  ultimately controlled their working conditions and was therefore obligated to negotiate a contract that would improve their pay and make the work less taxing.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  has investigated some of the cases and issued at least one complaint finding the drivers to be \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees and accusing the company of breaking the law by failing to bargain with them.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  said in a statement that workers at other \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouses were prepared to join the strike. The largest group at \uc2 Amazon\uc2  represented by the union works at a Staten Island warehouse known as JFK8, which employs more than 5,000 people. Employees at the warehouse voted to unionize in 2022, but the company has yet to bargain with them and is challenging the election outcome.\par \par \uc2 Workers involved in the strike say it could extend into early next week, perhaps into Christmas, but it's unclear how big an impact the walkout will have on \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's holiday deliveries.\par \par \uc2 The company has hundreds of delivery hubs across the country, and 10 or more in some of the largest urban areas. It has said that if one delivery hub experiences delays or driver shortages, the company can seamlessly shift packages to another hub nearby.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has also filled in gaps in its regular delivery fleet by summoning individuals through an on-demand \uc2 Uber\uc2 -like program known as Amazon Flex, in which people use their own cars to deliver packages.\par \par \uc2 Former delivery hub managers say these methods have helped the company reliably avoid disruptions in the past, though the ability to navigate a strike is likely to diminish during the holiday season, when the network has less spare capacity.\par \par \uc2 At the delivery hubs, \uc2 Amazon\uc2  generally hires contracting firms to take packages to customers. The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  has organized the drivers who work there by asking them to sign authorization cards. The union typically proceeds by trying to organize individual contracting firms rather than an entire complex at once. In most cases, the owners of the contracting firms have yet to recognize the union and there have not been elections.\par \par \uc2 ''What you see here are almost entirely outsiders -- not \uc2 Amazon\uc2  employees or partners -- and the suggestion otherwise is just another lie from the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2 ,'' \uc2 Amazon\uc2  said in a statement, referring to people picketing outside the delivery hubs. ''The truth is that they were unable to get enough support from our employees and partners and have brought in outsiders to come and harass and intimidate our team.''\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  had set a deadline of Dec. 15 for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  to begin negotiating with the drivers and warehouse employees. It initiated the strike after \uc2 Amazon\uc2  failed to do so.\par \par \uc2 ''If your package is delayed during the holidays, you can blame \uc2 Amazon\uc2 's insatiable greed,'' Sean O'Brien, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  president, said in a statement. ''We gave \uc2 Amazon\uc2  a clear deadline to come to the table and do right by our members. They ignored it.''\par \par \uc2 Three of the seven hubs are in Southern California, and the other four are in Queens; Atlanta; San Francisco; and Skokie, Ill., near Chicago.\par \par \uc2 Outside the \uc2 Amazon\uc2  warehouse DBK4 in the Maspeth section of Queens, more than 200 people were walking the picket line at around 10 a.m.; about half appeared to have jobs connected to \uc2 Amazon\uc2 . They wore blue vests and carried signs that included slogans like ''\uc2 Amazon\uc2  is unfair'' and ''Obey the law.'' One protester led chants like ''Shut it down!'' over a megaphone.\par \par \uc2 The picket line was set up near the exit where delivery vans leave, and picketers tried to stop vehicles from leaving several times. By 11 a.m., police officers had set up barricades on the sidewalk, and more than a dozen \uc2 Amazon\uc2  delivery vans were able to exit. An hour later, the crowd had thinned, but dozens of people continued to picket.\par \par \uc2 Antonio Lopez, a 27-year-old driver who has delivered \uc2 Amazon\uc2  packages for more than three years, said he wanted better pay and working conditions, and for the company to support his career development.\par \par \uc2 ''Anywhere is hard work, but people deserve to be paid for their hard work,'' said Mr. Lopez, who earns around $23 per hour and is completing a certificate as a medical technician.\par \par \uc2 Drivers have complained that \uc2 Amazon\uc2  pushes them to deliver hundreds of packages a day with little margin for error, while monitoring their movements and driving habits. Some say they resort to urinating in bottles so that they don't fall behind schedule.\par \par \uc2 Christian Santana, who has delivered goods for \uc2 Amazon\uc2  for more than two years, said the work conditions had taxed his physical health. ''The workload never goes down,'' Mr. Santana said, adding that he has frequently had to urinate in a bottle while delivering packages.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  has said that while it sets safety and quality standards, the contractors that directly employ the drivers are responsible for enforcing them.\par \par \uc2 Looming over the conflict between the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  and the company is the upcoming change in the federal government. Under President Biden, the \uc2 National Labor Relations Board\uc2  aggressively enforced labor laws and brought many cases against employers.\par \par \uc2 But the labor board was far less sympathetic to unions' claims on these issues during the first administration of President-elect Donald J. Trump. And most union leaders expect Mr. Trump's labor board appointees to be relatively unsympathetic to their claims during his second administration as well. That may be prompting some unions to pressure employers and seek concessions before Mr. Trump's inauguration on Jan. 20.\par \par \uc2 Mr. O'Brien, the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  leader, spoke at the Republican convention this summer, and the union remained neutral in the presidential election -- a break from recent campaign cycles. This appeared to give him some influence with Mr. Trump, who has tapped a more union-friendly candidate to run his Labor Department than most Republican presidents have in recent memory.\par \par \uc2 But the labor board, not the department, has much more direct influence over workers' ability to organize into unions, and it is unclear how much input Mr. O'Brien or the \uc2 Teamsters\uc2  will have on appointments to the board.\par \par \uc2 Amazon\uc2  and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , which was founded and is led by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , a close adviser to Mr. Trump, have both challenged the constitutionality of the labor board in federal court. The cases are active.\par \par \uc2 Document NYTF000020241220ekck0003i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw284\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal4260\pichgoal600
